d be cmp-identical to the b5b5cad3 copy.\n- Do not project row 23 yet. A later Testing snapshot has to observe the restore first.\n- If the XML shows something other than a compiled red run naming a row-23 identity (for example a survivor, or a different failure set), record the observed outcome truthfully, still restore the file, and stop. Do not apply the next mutant in that case.\n\n**(4) Only if row 23 is a confirmed kill: apply the dedicated row-28 mutant** (REQ-CDME-ASSURANCE × depth-class://invariant, identity \"UAT-ASSR-INV: moving further past a threshold never passes and a report passes only when every check passes\").\n- Use the locus test-design §7 plans: the AssuranceReport.passed every-check conjunction. First find which selected main source file defines it.\n- The locus and mechanism must differ from row 26's AtMost.admits inversion at AssuranceService.scala:22.\n- Before editing, confirm that the target file's baseline digest equals its b5b5cad3 copy. AssuranceService.scala is 7cacd34a…/3257; if the conjunction is in cdme-core package.scala, that file is ae7cdbbe…/9131.\n- Record the mutant digest and length, the exact restore obligation, the compile-safety reasoning, and the predicted red and collateral tests. Mark all predictions as unobserved.\n\n**Constraints**\n- Touch no test, comment, build file, XML or test-execution-result.json.\n- Make no kill claim beyond what the admitted XML shows.\n- Disclose any out-of-scope reads, partial reads of mandatory inputs, and possible incidental writes.\n- Avoid git commands, because they may refresh the outer repository's index.",
